Well Ogg the caveman with his little tame dog Ugg go down the stairs
to dungeon level 3.  The very first move that Ugg makes is to step
on a sleeping gas trap.  Ogg picks up some gold and goes back up the
stairs to level 2 leaving Ugg behind still asleep.  Ogg spends 
some time on level 2 and uses his gold in the potion shop on that level.
He spends a sufficient amount of time on level 2 so that there is
a fair chance his pet will become wild.  At any rate, Ogg goes back
to level 3 and finds his pet still tame yet still asleep.  Although
Ogg is a caveman and cavemen aren't too bright; he understands that
  (very minor spoiler)
monsters are only updated when the character is on their level.  So
he was not suprised to find Ugg still asleep.  He figures he will
wait a few turns for Ugg to wake up.  He waits and waits and waits.
Ugg doesn't move.  Ogg #chats to his asleep pet.  "Ugg seems not
to notice you."  Ogg kicks down a locked door making all kinds of noise
in that room.  Ugg doesn't move.  Ogg, a little upset by his good
for nothing dog,  throws tripe at Ugg.  "The tripe ration misses Ugg"
Ugg still sleeps.  Ogg eventually does something stupid, typical
of cavemen, and gets himself killed.  So he never got around to
kicking his dog or attacking it to try to wake it.  Wandering monsters
didn't attack Ugg even though they had the oppertunity.  (I suspect
this is normal though, since the pet seems to initiate combat with
monsters.)   Anyways this appears to be some type of bug with
nethack 3.0j  I spent hundreds of turns on that level and the dog never
did wake up.  Anyone else ever run across this before?

Douglas Gremaux

PS  I vote for Ugg (permanently asleep)  as the most useless pet
in the game.  After all at least a yellow light blows up on some 
monster.


